1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,739
This is a ruin.

2
00:00:02,189 --> 00:00:07,407
Three rooms, two tunnels, older than anyone who could have built it.

3
00:00:07,857 --> 00:00:13,509
I did not model it and I did not place a single rock.

4
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:17,437
I wrote down where the empty space is.

5
00:00:17,887 --> 00:00:19,626
Today you write yours.

6
00:00:20,826 --> 00:00:24,739
A ruin is hollow, so you describe the hollow.

7
00:00:25,189 --> 00:00:29,537
A chamber is a ball of open space: a room.

8
00:00:29,987 --> 00:00:35,639
A passage is a tube of open space between two chambers: a tunnel.

9
00:00:36,089 --> 00:00:44,785
A box is a block with flat sides: a built room, and you will add one yourself at the end.

10
00:00:45,235 --> 00:00:48,278
Whatever you do not describe is wall.

11
00:00:49,478 --> 00:00:54,696
A new section, and its key has to be the word relics.

12
00:00:55,146 --> 00:01:00,363
Then the ruin: a name for people, a key for the file.

13
00:01:00,813 --> 00:01:02,117
And one field.

14
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:06,046
Loc is where it stands: across, height, along.

15
00:01:06,496 --> 00:01:09,539
The station is at zero, zero, zero.

16
00:01:09,989 --> 00:01:12,598
The hulk is nine thousand along.

17
00:01:13,048 --> 00:01:17,396
So this is past the hulk, on the same line.

18
00:01:17,846 --> 00:01:21,324
The sentence underneath is a note to myself.

19
00:01:21,774 --> 00:01:23,948
No player ever reads it.

20
00:01:25,148 --> 00:01:29,496
Three hashes again, the same as the ruin. Not four.

21
00:01:29,946 --> 00:01:39,511
A room is not written inside the ruin; it is written beside it, and this line says whose it is. Relic: hollow.

22
00:01:39,961 --> 00:01:42,135
The key, not the name.

23
00:01:42,585 --> 00:01:44,324
Then Chamber, four numbers.

24
00:01:44,774 --> 00:01:52,600
The first three say where, measured from the ruin, so zero zero zero is the ruin's own spot.

25
00:01:53,050 --> 00:01:55,224
The fourth is the radius.

26
00:01:55,674 --> 00:01:58,283
Nine hundred, so eighteen hundred across.

27
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:01,341
My ship is about a hundred.

28
00:02:02,541 --> 00:02:06,889
The Nave is three thousand to one side, and bigger.

29
00:02:07,339 --> 00:02:11,687
And it has a passage: to mouth, radius three fifty.

30
00:02:12,137 --> 00:02:13,876
That is the tunnel.

31
00:02:14,326 --> 00:02:17,370
I write it once, on either room.

32
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:24,776
The Vault is twenty-eight hundred further along from the Nave, with a passage back to it.

33
00:02:25,226 --> 00:02:27,835
So the ruin turns a corner.

34
00:02:28,285 --> 00:02:32,198
Keep neighbours within about thirty-five hundred of each other.

35
00:02:33,398 --> 00:02:37,746
With the file in front: Control Shift P, Relic Plan.

36
00:02:38,196 --> 00:02:44,283
There it is, drawn from the file, and the game is not even running.

37
00:02:44,733 --> 00:02:46,472
Top looks straight down.

38
00:02:46,922 --> 00:02:49,096
Each square is a thousand.

39
00:02:49,546 --> 00:02:54,763
Hover a room for its size; hover a tunnel for its length.

40
00:02:55,213 --> 00:02:59,126
Now click the Vault and make it eight hundred.

41
00:02:59,576 --> 00:03:02,620
Look at the file: one line changed.

42
00:03:03,070 --> 00:03:06,983
The picture and the file are the same thing.

43
00:03:07,433 --> 00:03:09,607
Undo, and it is back.

44
00:03:10,807 --> 00:03:13,850
The file says what the ruin is.

45
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:29,517
And this line, which was in your mission from the day you made it, builds every ruin the file holds: the space, the rock around it, whatever is inside, and its name on the map.

46
00:03:29,967 --> 00:03:32,141
You do not touch it.

47
00:03:32,591 --> 00:03:36,504
No ruin in the file, and it does nothing.

48
00:03:37,704 --> 00:03:38,704
Lint. Clean.

49
00:03:39,154 --> 00:03:45,241
A passage to a room that does not exist: it tells me, by name.

50
00:03:45,691 --> 00:03:51,343
Fix that one, because with it the game builds no ruin at all.

51
00:03:51,793 --> 00:03:54,837
Now a fourth hash on the Vault.

52
00:03:55,287 --> 00:03:57,896
The plan still shows three rooms.

53
00:03:58,346 --> 00:04:07,041
Lint is not fooled: this room is nested under the one above it, and the game will not read it.

54
00:04:07,491 --> 00:04:11,404
Three hashes on the ruin, three on every room.

55
00:04:11,854 --> 00:04:14,028
One thing lint cannot see.

56
00:04:14,478 --> 00:04:21,435
Take the Loc line away, and lint is clean, because it cannot know where you meant.

57
00:04:21,885 --> 00:04:26,233
The ruin would be built on top of the station.

58
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:27,987
Keep the line.

59
00:04:29,187 --> 00:04:31,361
Past the hulk: The Hollow.

60
00:04:31,811 --> 00:04:35,289
That marker is the middle of the Mouth.

61
00:04:35,739 --> 00:04:37,913
And this is my wall.

62
00:04:38,363 --> 00:04:42,276
It is scenery today; it will not stop me.

63
00:04:42,726 --> 00:04:46,204
Through the tunnel, and this is the Nave.

64
00:04:47,404 --> 00:04:53,926
Add a fourth room, and make it a box: a built room with flat walls.

65
00:04:54,376 --> 00:04:58,289
Join it by overlapping the room next to it.

66
00:04:58,739 --> 00:05:07,870
Then move it away, watch lint tell you the ruin is in two pieces, and join it again with a passage.

67
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:12,667
Next time we decide what these walls are made of.
